15385      data Cheese;
15386      do Additive = 1 to 4;
15387      do y = 1 to 9;
15388      input freq @@;
15389      output;
15390      end;
15391      end;
15392      label y='Taste Rating';
15393      datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.CHEESE has 36 observations and 3 variables.

15398      ;
15399      ods graphics on;
15400      proc logistic data=Cheese plots(only)=oddsratio(range=clip);
15401      freq freq;
15402      class Additive (param=ref ref='4');
15403      model y=Additive / covb nooddsratio;
15404      oddsratio Additive;
15405      effectplot / polybar;
15406      title 'Multiple Response Cheese Tasting Experiment';
15407      run;

NOTE: PROC LOGISTIC is fitting the cumulative logit model. The probabilities modeled are summed over the responses having the lower Ordered Values in the 
      Response Profile table. Use the response variable option DESCENDING if you want to reverse the assignment of Ordered Values to the response levels.
NOTE: Convergence criterion (GCONV=1E-8) satisfied.
NOTE: There were 36 observations read from the data set WORK.CHEESE.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE LOGISTIC printed page 1255.

15408      proc logistic data=Cheese
15409      plots(only)=effect(x=y sliceby=additive connect yrange=(0,0.4));
15410      freq freq;
15411      class Additive (param=ref ref='4');
15412      model y=Additive / nooddsratio link=alogit;
15413      oddsratio Additive;
15414      title 'Multiple Response Cheese Tasting Experiment';
15415      run;

NOTE: PROC LOGISTIC is fitting the adjacent-category logit model. The logits modeled contrast each response level against the next higher Ordered Value. Use 
      the response variable option DESCENDING if you want to contrast higher Ordered Values against lower Ordered Values.
NOTE: Convergence criterion (GCONV=1E-8) satisfied.
NOTE: There were 36 observations read from the data set WORK.CHEESE.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE LOGISTIC printed page 1256.

